==Enemy==
Capy has huge health and DPS, a 15% chance for a [[Critical Hit]] at a surprisingly high 335 range, and a low money drop. You won't be able to tank her attacks as she'll chomp through even the strongest tanks in seconds, and that's if she doesn't put you into a budget deficit first. Her biggest weakness is that she is a single-target attacker, so meatshielding and using ranged units is an effective way to counter her.

==Strategy==
Capy's Single Attack makes her very easy to stall using meatshields when she is alone. However, if she is supported by powerful area attackers like [[J.K. Bun Bun]], the attackers can wipe out all your meatshields while Capy will annihilate your stronger cat units (notably in [[Oil Platform]] and [[Morning Rush Hour]]).

Capies are usually fought in multiples. With the right support, they can actually push, so try using the [[Cat Cannon]] to sync their attack animations. This is particularly important in Morning Rush Hour, where you have to use a "ranged meatshield" such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] to bait them out; see Lucas IV's [https://youtu.be/e8YVxHYGcO4 video] on this strategy for more information.

There is no difference between [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and variants versus other 75¢ meatshields, as they all get killed in one hit. Therefore, bringing 75¢ meatshields (or [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]], who can usually survive even several Capies at once) is recommended as they'll absorb a hit for half the cost. If she is supported by a backliner/pusher who can instantly wipe cheaper meatshields, such as the [[Camelle]] in [[A Day of Reckoning]], you'll still need your Erasers, though. Another efficient meatshield option is using units that survive lethal strikes, such as [[Kyubey Cat (Rare Cat)|Kyubey Cat]] and [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]]. Capies are also extremely vulnerable to [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], as its anti-Red ability combined with its Long Distance AoE attacks can easily wipe even huge stacks of Capies in less than half a minute.

"Strong" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]] on [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] work greatly against a single Capy, and fantastically against multiple, if meatshielded properly.

